+    // commit actually carries different props for it. A React commit is built
+    // from React's own copy of the tree, which never holds Reanimated's values,
+    // so every view React rendered still compares different and is re-applied
+    // as before. A state-only commit (Android's ScrollView reports its offset
+    // as state on EVERY scroll frame) is cloned from the committed tree, whose
+    // nodes already carry the registry's values; re-applying them there
+    // re-mounted every view Reanimated had ever animated, every frame of a
+    // fling, re-recording their drawing and re-rasterising SVGs.
     propsRegistry_->for_each(
         [&](const ShadowNodeFamily &family, const folly::dynamic &props) {
+          const auto *newNode = findInTree(family, *newRootShadowNode);
